sentences.t:
Aquim parto de vos commo de malos e de traydores.
Iré con vuestra graçia, don Elvira e doña Sol;
poco preçio las nuevas de los de Carrión.

sentences.l:
Here-myself I-part from you as from wicked-ones and from traitors.
I-will-go with your grace, don Elvira and doña Sol;
little I-prize the renown of those of Carrión.

sentences.t:
Esto les ha dicho, e el moro se tornó;
teniendo iva armas al troçir de Salón;
qu[o]mmo de buen seso a Molina se tornó.

sentences.l:
This to-them he-has said, and the Moor himself turned;
holding he-went arms at-the crossing of Salón;
as (one) of good sense to Molina himself returned.

sentences.t:
a ssiniestro dexan Ati[en]ça, una peña muy fu[o]rt,
la sierra de Miedes passáronla estoz,
por los Montes Claros aguijan a espolón;

sentences.l:
on left they-leave Ati[en]ça, a crag very strong,
the sierra of Miedes they-passed-it then,
through the Montes Claros they-spur at spur;

sentences.t:
assiniestro dexan a Griza que Álamos pobló,
allí son caños do a Elpha ençerró;
a diestro dexan aSant Estevan, mas ca[d]e alu[o]n.

sentences.l:
on-left they-leave Griza, which Álamos settled,
there are caves where Elpha he-shut-up;
on right they-leave Sant Estevan, but it-lies far.

sentences.t:
Fallaron un vergel con una linpia fu[o]nt;
mandan fincar la tienda ifantes de Carrión,
con quantos que ellos traen i yazen essa noch,

sentences.l:
They-found an orchard with a clear spring;
they-order to-pitch the tent Infantes of Carrión,
with as-many that they bring there they-lie that night,

sentences.t:
Atan malos enssienplos non fagades sobre nos:
si nos fuéremos majadas, abiltaredes a vos;
retraer vos lo an en vistas o en cortes.”

sentences.l:
So wicked deeds not may-you-do upon us:
if we should-be beaten, you-will-debase yourselves;
to-cast-up to-you it they-will in meetings or in courts.”
